note seed/node/code.om -- the Omega Node coding workflow (DRA-290): the
note round40 repair protocol (read, check, edit, check again, answer) driven
note by the own Omega model through the Node's scheduler, authority and
note journal, under live operator control (DRA-291). OM-2. Compose after
note seed/net/http.om, seed/net/notls.om, transport.om, pool.om, super.om,
note sched.om, seed/authority/action.om, journal.om, auth.om, view.om,
note seed/node/gram.om, and before one program with fn main (code-main.om
note or code-test.om).
note Processes. The creator holds every objective's state; it alone reads
note model output and decides. Two workers run granted jobs, each one child
note process in its own process group (auth_wtool): omnode-infer for a model
note turn, omnode-tool for read_file, omega_check and replace_text, and a
note review (a fresh omnode-tool check of the edited file). A job's input is
note the packed argv the creator published on the objective's topic bit;
note the worker proposes it, the creator grants it (generation, staleness,
note cancellation, journal START), the worker runs it and returns the
note child's record (OMNI1 or OMNT1, at most 3968 bytes) with the outcome.
note One inference at a time: the provider is a single local ollm serve.
note A turn has 160 new tokens (as round40 sampled) and 900 s, since the CPU
note server needs minutes for a long prompt on a shared host.
note Policy, as round40 repair.py jobs_run: at most 7 model turns; the action
note must name the objective's path; read_file only when unread, omega_check
note only when read or edited, replace_text only when failed, whose old text
note must occur exactly once in the source the model was shown and whose
note result must stay in the repair grammar (checked here before the grant);
note Tests passed. only when the last check passed (then a review job runs),
note File not found. only when the read found no file. Anything else ends
note the objective as failed; nothing is repaired or retried.
note Results: 1 PASS; failures 10 action not valid in its state, 11 wrong
note path, 12 out of turns, 13 edit refused, 14 Tests passed. unverified,
note 15 the file differs from the workflow's source, 16 inference failed
note (exit status in the event line; no fallback), 17 tool failed, 18
note malformed record, 19 cancelled, 20 prompt too long, 21 outcome UNKNOWN,
note 22 job input lost, 23 refused by the authority.
note Restart: the journal releases what the last creator left (auth_recover);
note jobs still waiting for input are cancelled; an objective whose result
note the journal holds (RESULT) is reported with it again and never resumed;
note every other objective resumes from the durable workspace in state
note unread, with the model turns already performed counted against its
note budget and its job ids continuing; the committed operator commands are
note then applied again in order to the objectives still open.
note Operator (DRA-291): the creator writes a snapshot of its state and an
note event per change to view.om's page every loop, and takes one posted
note command per loop. A command is checked against the version the
note operator saw (stale when its target changed since), committed in the
note journal (OPER; pause and resume first through auth_pause), then acted
note on and acknowledged: pause and resume, cancel an objective (its job in
note flight is cancelled through the authority and the objective ends 19),
note set its turn budget (0..7; out of turns ends 12), or redirect it to
note another goal (its job in flight is cancelled and it starts over from
note unread). A tool job the authority refuses ends its objective with 23.
note Events on stdout, one line each: CWP (prompt) and CWR (model text) are
note followed by their bytes and a newline; CWE job events; CWO results;
note CWV the operator view's port once it listens.
const CWOBJ ulong 4
text cwtask "Task: "
text cwfile "\nFile: "
text cwgoal "\nGoal: "
text cwstat "\nState: "
text cwsrcl "Source:\n"
text cwtres "Tool result: "
text cwansw "Answer:\n"
text cwnl "\n"
text cwsp " "
text cwgl1 "calc starts with x and adds "
text cwgl2 " exactly "
text cwgl3 " times in a for loop. main calls calc with "
text cwgl4 "calc returns x "
text cwplus "plus "
text cwtims "times "
text cwgl5 ". main calls calc with "
text cwdot "."
text cwsun "unread"
text cwsrd "read"
text cwsfl "failed"
text cwsed "edited"
text cwsck "checked"
text cwsms "missing"
text cwvrd "read"
text cwvck "check"
text cwvrp "replace"
text cwmax "160"
text cwdl "900"
text cwo "/o"
text cwadd "add"
text cwmul "mul"
text cwloop "loop"
text cwhi "OMNI1 "
text cwht "OMNT1 "
text cwep "CWP "
text cwer "CWR "
text cwee "CWE "
text cweo "CWO "
text cwpass "PASS"
text cwfail "FAIL"
text cwsum "CWSUM pass="
text cwsumf " fail="
global cwcf uchar 8192
global cwcl ulong 8
global cwno ulong 1
global cwos uchar 2048
global cwob ulong 128
global cwsrc uchar 16384
global cwobs uchar 4096
global cwcan uchar 16384
global cwinf ulong 1
global cwgot ulong 64
global cwt0 ulong 4
global cwtk ulong 2
global cwpv ulong 1
global cwql ulong 1
global cwtu ulong 1
text cwcwv "CWV "
note Objective words shown in the view's rows, as characters '0' + word.
text cwvw "012367@9:<ABC;"

note ======== objective words: cwob[32 i + w]: 0 kind (1 add, 2 mul, 3 loop),
note 1 K, 2 N, 3 A, 4 path length, 5 task length, 6 state (0 unread, 1 read,
note 2 failed, 3 edited, 4 checked, 5 missing), 7 model turns, 8 verified,
note 9 phase (0 needs a turn, 1 inference, 2 tool, 3 review, 4 finished), 10
note job in flight, 11 next job seq, 12 result, 13 source length, 14
note observation length, 15 candidate length, 16 turn budget (7 unless the
note operator set one), 17 view version of its last change, 18 redirect
note waiting for the job in flight, 19 operator cancel.
fn cw_g i ulong w ulong to ulong
ret get cwob add mul i 32 w
end

fn cw_s i ulong w ulong v ulong to void
put cwob add mul i 32 w v
end

note ======== bytes

fn cw_out o view uchar * n ulong to void
p = ulong 0
for it ulong 65536
if ge p n
ret
end
r = write 1 o p sub n p
if le r 0
ret
end
p = add p ulong r
end
end

note Append a to o at p; past 4096 bytes the result is 5000 (overflow), and
note an overflowed p stays overflowed.
fn cw_cat o edit uchar 4096 p ulong a view uchar * to ulong
if gt add p len a 4096
ret 5000
end
for i ulong len a
put o add p i get a i
end
ret add p len a
end

fn cw_dec o edit uchar 4096 p ulong v ulong to ulong
d = new uchar 24 0
k = ulong 0
x = v
for i ulong 24
put d k uchar add 48 rem x 10
k = add k 1
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
if gt add p k 4096
ret 5000
end
for j ulong k
put o add p j get d sub sub k j 1
end
ret add p k
end

fn cw_eq a view uchar * b view uchar * to bool
if ne len a len b
ret false
end
for i ulong len a
if ne get a i get b i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note Occurrences of a in s, without overlap.
fn cw_count s view uchar * a view uchar * to ulong
c = ulong 0
i = ulong 0
for it ulong add len s 1
if gt add i len a len s
ret c
end
if cw_eq view part s i len a a
c = add c 1
i = add i len a
else
i = add i 1
end
end
ret c
end

note ======== prompt (repair.py prompt and goal)

fn cw_sname o edit uchar 4096 p ulong st ulong to ulong
if eq st 0
ret cw_cat o p cwsun
end
if eq st 1
ret cw_cat o p cwsrd
end
if eq st 2
ret cw_cat o p cwsfl
end
if eq st 3
ret cw_cat o p cwsed
end
if eq st 4
ret cw_cat o p cwsck
end
ret cw_cat o p cwsms
end

fn cw_goal o edit uchar 4096 p ulong i ulong to ulong
if eq cw_g i 0 3
q = cw_cat o p cwgl1
q = cw_dec o q cw_g i 1
q = cw_cat o q cwgl2
q = cw_dec o q cw_g i 2
q = cw_cat o q cwgl3
q = cw_dec o q cw_g i 3
ret cw_cat o q cwdot
end
q = cw_cat o p cwgl4
if eq cw_g i 0 1
q = cw_cat o q cwplus
else
q = cw_cat o q cwtims
end
q = cw_dec o q cw_g i 1
q = cw_cat o q cwgl5
q = cw_dec o q cw_g i 3
ret cw_cat o q cwdot
end

note Globals are never call arguments, so text kept in them is copied into
note a local first. sel: 0 path, 1 task, 2 source, 3 observation, 4 edit
note candidate of objective i; 10 + k config slot k. The length.
fn cw_ld d edit uchar 4096 sel ulong i ulong to ulong
if le sel 1
n = cw_g i add 4 sel
b = add mul i 512 mul sel 128
for j ulong n bound 4096
put d j get cwos add b j
end
ret n
end
if eq sel 2
n2 = cw_g i 13
for j2 ulong n2 bound 4096
put d j2 get cwsrc add mul i 4096 j2
end
ret n2
end
if eq sel 3
n3 = cw_g i 14
for j3 ulong n3 bound 1024
put d j3 get cwobs add mul i 1024 j3
end
ret n3
end
if eq sel 4
n4 = cw_g i 15
for j4 ulong n4 bound 4096
put d j4 get cwcan add mul i 4096 j4
end
ret n4
end
k = sub sel 10
n5 = get cwcl k
for j5 ulong n5 bound 1024
put d j5 get cwcf add mul k 1024 j5
end
ret n5
end

note Append loaded item sel of objective i to o at p.
fn cw_catl o edit uchar 4096 p ulong sel ulong i ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 4096 0
n = cw_ld t sel i
ret cw_cat o p view part t 0 n
end

note The prompt of objective i in its current state; length, 5000 overflow.
fn cw_prmt o edit uchar 4096 i ulong to ulong
p = cw_cat o 0 cwtask
p = cw_catl o p 1 i
p = cw_cat o p cwfile
p = cw_catl o p 0 i
p = cw_cat o p cwgoal
p = cw_goal o p i
p = cw_cat o p cwstat
p = cw_sname o p cw_g i 6
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
if gt cw_g i 13 0
p = cw_cat o p cwsrcl
p = cw_catl o p 2 i
end
if gt cw_g i 14 0
p = cw_cat o p cwtres
p = cw_catl o p 3 i
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
end
ret cw_cat o p cwansw
end

note ======== packed argv (count, then length-prefixed arguments)

fn cw_arg d edit uchar 4096 p ulong a view uchar * to ulong
if gt add add p 2 len a 4096
ret 5000
end
c = add or ulong get d 0 shl ulong get d 1 8 1
put d 0 uchar and c 255
put d 1 uchar shr c 8
put d p uchar and len a 255
put d add p 1 uchar shr len a 8
for i ulong len a
put d add add p 2 i get a i
end
ret add add p 2 len a
end

note Append loaded item sel of objective i to d as one argument.
fn cw_argl d edit uchar 4096 p ulong sel ulong i ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 4096 0
n = cw_ld t sel i
ret cw_arg d p view part t 0 n
end

fn cw_cfg d edit uchar 4096 p ulong k ulong to ulong
ret cw_argl d p add 10 k 0
end

fn cw_narg d edit uchar 4096 p ulong v ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 4096 0
n = cw_dec t 0 v
ret cw_arg d p view part t 0 n
end

note WORK/o<i>, the objective's private compile directory.
fn cw_wdir t edit uchar 4096 i ulong to ulong
p = cw_catl t 0 14 0
p = cw_cat t p cwo
ret cw_dec t p i
end

note ======== events

fn cw_ev i ulong id ulong what ulong v ulong to void
o = new uchar 4096 0
p = cw_cat o 0 cwee
p = cw_dec o p i
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p id
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p what
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p v
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
cw_out o p
cw_s i 17 vw_ev 1 i what id v
end

note A framed transcript record: tag i turn n, newline, the bytes, newline.
fn cw_rec tag ulong i ulong b view uchar * to void
o = new uchar 4096 0
p = ulong 0
if eq tag 0
p = cw_cat o 0 cwep
else
p = cw_cat o 0 cwer
end
p = cw_dec o p i
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p cw_g i 7
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p len b
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
cw_out o p
cw_out b len b
cw_out cwnl 1
end

note Objective i finished with result r (1 PASS, else the failure): RESULT
note is made durable first (a result the journal refuses is still reported
note for this run; a restart then resumes that objective), then published.
fn cw_end i ulong r ulong to void
x = jn_result i r cw_g i 7
cw_pub i r
end

note Publish objective i's result r: its CWO line and view event.
fn cw_pub i ulong r ulong to void
o = new uchar 4096 0
cw_s i 12 r
cw_s i 9 4
p = cw_cat o 0 cweo
p = cw_dec o p i
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
if eq r 1
p = cw_cat o p cwpass
else
p = cw_cat o p cwfail
end
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p r
p = cw_cat o p cwsp
p = cw_dec o p cw_g i 7
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
cw_out o p
cw_s i 17 vw_ev 2 i 0 r cw_g i 7
end

note ======== creator: issuing jobs

note Admit job kind (1 inference, 2 read, 3 check, 4 replace, 5 review) of
note objective i with input pk[0, pn), then publish the input on the
note objective's topic, which makes the job ready. The job id, or 0 when it
note was not admitted. A refused inference is asked for again at the next
note step (admission refusals are counted for the view). A refused tool job
note ends the objective with 23: it cannot be a full queue (a tool job is
note issued only after its objective's previous job left the queue, so it
note takes that job's place), and nothing is left waiting unseen.
fn cw_issue c long i ulong kind ulong pk view uchar 4096 pn ulong to ulong
s = cw_g i 11
if ge s 99
cw_end i 20
ret 0
end
id = add add mul add i 1 1000 mul s 10 kind
fl = ulong 1
if eq kind 4
fl = 0
end
t = shl ulong 1 i
j = jn_admit id t fl
if lt j 0
if eq j neg long 2
vw_cnt 0 add vw_cget 0 1
end
if ne kind 1
cw_end i 23
end
ret 0
end
cw_s i 11 add s 1
v = sched_publish c t pk pn
if le v 0
x = auth_cancel c ulong j
cw_end i 22
ret 0
end
cw_s i 10 id
put cwt0 i ulong monons
cw_ev i id 1 kind
ret id
end

note Start objective i's next model turn: the prompt as the only input.
fn cw_turn c long i ulong to void
pr = new uchar 4096 0
pk = new uchar 4096 0
n = cw_prmt pr i
if gt n 3800
cw_end i 20
ret
end
p = cw_cfg pk 2 0
p = cw_cfg pk p 6
p = cw_arg pk p cwmax
p = cw_arg pk p cwdl
p = cw_arg pk p view part pr 0 n
if gt p 4096
cw_end i 20
ret
end
id = cw_issue c i 1 pk p
if gt id 0
cw_s i 7 add cw_g i 7 1
cw_s i 9 1
put cwinf 0 add i 1
cw_rec 0 i view part pr 0 n
end
end

note TOOL verb ROOT PATH into pk; the length.
fn cw_targ pk edit uchar 4096 i ulong vb ulong to ulong
p = cw_cfg pk 2 1
if eq vb 2
p = cw_arg pk p cwvrd
end
if or eq vb 3 eq vb 5
p = cw_arg pk p cwvck
end
if eq vb 4
p = cw_arg pk p cwvrp
end
p = cw_cfg pk p 3
ret cw_argl pk p 0 i
end

note A read (2), check (3) or review (5) job for objective i.
fn cw_tool c long i ulong kind ulong to void
pk = new uchar 4096 0
t = new uchar 4096 0
p = cw_targ pk i kind
if ne kind 2
n = cw_wdir t i
p = cw_arg pk p view part t 0 n
p = cw_cfg pk p 2
p = cw_narg pk p cw_g i 0
p = cw_narg pk p cw_g i 1
p = cw_narg pk p cw_g i 2
p = cw_narg pk p cw_g i 3
end
id = cw_issue c i kind pk p
if gt id 0
cw_s i 9 2
if eq kind 5
cw_s i 9 3
end
end
end

note A replace job for objective i: old (h5 bytes at b[o]) and new (h6
note bytes after it) as the model gave them.
fn cw_repl c long i ulong b view uchar 4096 o ulong h view ulong 16 to void
pk = new uchar 4096 0
p = cw_targ pk i 4
p = cw_arg pk p view part b o get h 5
p = cw_arg pk p view part b add o get h 5 get h 6
id = cw_issue c i 4 pk p
if gt id 0
cw_s i 9 2
end
end

note ======== creator: records

note Parse k decimal fields of record b after the 6-byte tag into h[0..k);
note the offset after the header line, or 0 when malformed.
fn cw_hdr b view uchar 4096 k ulong h edit ulong 16 to ulong
p = ulong 6
for f ulong k
v = ulong 0
nd = ulong 0
for it ulong 12
c = ulong get b p
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
break
end
v = add mul v 10 sub c 48
nd = add nd 1
p = add p 1
end
if eq nd 0
ret 0
end
put h f v
c2 = get b p
if lt add f 1 k
if ne c2 32
ret 0
end
else
if ne c2 10
ret 0
end
end
p = add p 1
end
ret p
end

fn cw_tag b view uchar 4096 t view uchar * to bool
for i ulong 6
if ne get b i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end

note Objective i's model record b: the turn's action, checked against the
note state before anything is granted.
fn cw_ires c long i ulong b view uchar 4096 to void
h = new ulong 16 0
if not cw_tag b cwhi
cw_end i 18
ret
end
d = cw_hdr b 8 h
if or eq d 0 gt add add add add d get h 4 get h 5 get h 6 get h 7 3968
cw_end i 18
ret
end
x = add add add d get h 4 get h 5 get h 6
cw_rec 1 i view part b x get h 7
cw_ev i 0 2 get h 0
cw_act c i b d h
end

note The policy of repair.py jobs_run for action kind h[0], with path at
note b[d, d + h4), old after it (h5 bytes), new after that (h6 bytes).
fn cw_act c long i ulong b view uchar 4096 d ulong h view ulong 16 to void
u = new uchar 4096 0
un = cw_ld u 0 i
k = get h 0
st = cw_g i 6
if eq k 4
if and eq st 4 eq cw_g i 8 1
cw_tool c i 5
else
cw_end i 14
end
ret
end
if eq k 5
if eq st 5
cw_end i 1
else
cw_end i 10
end
ret
end
if or eq k 9 gt k 5
cw_end i 10
ret
end
if not cw_eq view part b d get h 4 view part u 0 un
cw_end i 11
ret
end
if and eq k 1 eq st 0
cw_tool c i 2
ret
end
if and eq k 2 or eq st 1 eq st 3
cw_tool c i 3
ret
end
if and eq k 3 eq st 2
cw_edit c i b add d get h 4 h
ret
end
cw_end i 10
end

note replace_text: the model's old must occur exactly once in the source it
note was shown and the result must stay in the grammar; the candidate is
note kept to compare with what the tool saved.
fn cw_edit c long i ulong b view uchar 4096 o ulong h view ulong 16 to void
u = new uchar 4096 0
un = cw_ld u 2 i
if ne cw_count view part u 0 un view part b o get h 5 1
cw_end i 13
ret
end
n = cw_cand i b o h
if gt n 3800
cw_end i 13
ret
end
cw_repl c i b o h
end

note The candidate source of objective i into cwcan: its length, or 5000
note when it is over 3800 bytes or outside the grammar.
fn cw_cand i ulong b view uchar 4096 o ulong h view ulong 16 to ulong
t = new uchar 4096 0
u = new uchar 4096 0
sn = cw_ld u 2 i
k = cw_at view part u 0 sn view part b o get h 5
p = cw_cat t 0 view part u 0 k
p = cw_cat t p view part b add o get h 5 get h 6
r = add k get h 5
p = cw_cat t p view part u r sub sn r
if gt p 3800
ret 5000
end
if not gr_src t p
ret 5000
end
cw_keep i t p
ret p
end

note The first occurrence of a in s (len s when none).
fn cw_at s view uchar * a view uchar * to ulong
for k ulong len s
if le add k len a len s
if cw_eq view part s k len a a
ret k
end
end
end
ret len s
end

fn cw_keep i ulong t view uchar 4096 n ulong to void
for j ulong n
put cwcan add mul i 4096 j get t j
end
cw_s i 15 n
end

note Objective i's tool record b for job kind.
fn cw_tres c long i ulong kind ulong b view uchar 4096 to void
h = new ulong 16 0
if not cw_tag b cwht
cw_end i 18
ret
end
d = cw_hdr b 3 h
if or eq d 0 or gt get h 1 1024 gt add add d get h 1 get h 2 3968
cw_end i 18
ret
end
st = get h 0
cw_ev i 0 3 st
if eq kind 2
cw_read i st b d h
ret
end
if eq kind 4
cw_saved i st b d h
ret
end
cw_chk i add mul kind 256 st b d h
end

note A tool record's observation is h1 bytes at b[d], its content the h2
note bytes after it. cw_same: the content equals loaded item sel.
fn cw_same i ulong sel ulong b view uchar 4096 d ulong h view ulong 16 to bool
u = new uchar 4096 0
un = cw_ld u sel i
ret cw_eq view part b add d get h 1 get h 2 view part u 0 un
end

note A check (kind 3) or review (5) record, ks = 256 kind + status: the file
note checked must be the source the workflow holds.
fn cw_chk i ulong ks ulong b view uchar 4096 d ulong h view ulong 16 to void
kind = shr ks 8
st = and ks 255
if not cw_same i 2 b d h
cw_end i 15
ret
end
if eq kind 5
if eq st 0
cw_end i 1
else
cw_end i 15
end
ret
end
if eq st 0
cw_s i 6 4
cw_s i 8 1
else
if ne st 6
cw_end i 17
ret
end
cw_s i 6 2
cw_s i 8 0
end
cw_seto i view part b d get h 1
cw_s i 9 0
end

fn cw_read i ulong st ulong b view uchar 4096 d ulong h view ulong 16 to void
if eq st 0
cw_s i 6 1
cw_setsrc i view part b add d get h 1 get h 2
cw_seto i view part b d get h 1
cw_s i 9 0
ret
end
if eq st 1
cw_s i 6 5
cw_s i 13 0
cw_seto i view part b d get h 1
cw_s i 9 0
ret
end
cw_end i 17
end

fn cw_saved i ulong st ulong b view uchar 4096 d ulong h view ulong 16 to void
if eq st 5
cw_end i 13
ret
end
if ne st 0
cw_end i 17
ret
end
if not cw_same i 4 b d h
cw_end i 15
ret
end
cw_s i 6 3
cw_s i 8 0
cw_setsrc i view part b add d get h 1 get h 2
cw_seto i view part b d get h 1
cw_s i 9 0
end

fn cw_setsrc i ulong f view uchar * to void
for j ulong len f
put cwsrc add mul i 4096 j get f j
end
cw_s i 13 len f
end

fn cw_seto i ulong o view uchar * to void
for j ulong len o
put cwobs add mul i 1024 j get o j
end
cw_s i 14 len o
end

note ======== creator: results

note A job of objective i in review: its result bytes are read before it is
note released and before the next auth_step, so no later job of the same
note worker (which needs a grant first) can have overwritten them.
fn cw_done c long j ulong id ulong to void
b = new uchar 4096 0
i = sub div id 1000 1
kind = rem id 10
if or ge i get cwno 0 ne id cw_g i 10
ret
end
r = sched_result get sjw j b
o = get sjout j
cw_s i 10 0
if eq kind 1
put cwinf 0 0
end
cw_ev i id 4 o
f = cw_fate o kind
if eq f 21
x = vw_ev 7 i 0 id 0
end
if cw_oper i
ret
end
if ne f 0
cw_end i f
ret
end
if eq kind 1
cw_ires c i b
ret
end
cw_tres c i kind b
end

note The failure for job outcome word o of a job of kind, 0 when its child
note ran and exited 0: refused 16 + verdict (cancelled, verdict 6: 19),
note input lost 90, not performed 1 (cancelled: 19), UNKNOWN 0 or a child
note killed by a signal (21), a nonzero exit (16 inference, 17 tool).
fn cw_fate o ulong kind ulong to ulong
lo = and o 255
if eq lo 2
ws = shr o 8
if ne and ws 127 0
ret 21
end
if eq and shr ws 8 255 0
ret 0
end
if eq kind 1
ret 16
end
ret 17
end
if or eq lo 1 eq lo 22
ret 19
end
if eq lo 0
ret 21
end
if eq lo 90
ret 22
end
ret 23
end

note Collect: every job in review is handled once, then released (again at
note the next step while its DONE is not yet durable). A job whose worker
note died mid-job (UNKNOWN) ends its objective; its slot stays UNKNOWN,
note since only the journal's recovery may settle what may have happened.
fn cw_coll c long to void
for j ulong 64
s = get sjst j
id = get sjid j
if and eq s 4 ne get cwgot j id
put cwgot j id
cw_done c j id
end
if eq s 4
x = jn_release j
end
if and eq s 6 ne get cwgot j id
put cwgot j id
cw_lost id
end
end
end

fn cw_lost id ulong to void
i = sub div id 1000 1
if and lt i get cwno 0 eq id cw_g i 10
cw_s i 10 0
if eq rem id 10 1
put cwinf 0 0
end
x = vw_ev 7 i 0 id 0
if not cw_oper i
cw_end i 21
end
end
end

note After objective i's job in flight finished or was lost: an operator
note cancel ends it (19); a redirect waiting for the job takes effect. True
note when one of them applied.
fn cw_oper i ulong to bool
if ne cw_g i 19 0
cw_end i 19
ret true
end
if ne cw_g i 18 0
cw_redo i
ret true
end
ret false
end

note Objective i starts over from unread with its new goal (a redirect):
note turns, budget and job ids continue.
fn cw_redo i ulong to void
cw_s i 18 0
cw_s i 6 0
cw_s i 8 0
cw_s i 9 0
cw_s i 13 0
cw_s i 14 0
cw_s i 15 0
end

note ======== creator: planning

note Start a turn for one objective that needs one (one inference in flight
note at a time); the test hook cwtk cancels an inference after ms. An
note objective out of its turn budget ends with 12.
fn cw_plan c long to void
cw_hook c
if gt get cwinf 0 0
ret
end
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
if and eq cw_g i 9 0 eq cw_g i 12 0
if ge cw_g i 7 cw_g i 16
cw_end i 12
else
cw_turn c i
ret
end
end
end
end

fn cw_hook c long to void
if ne get cwtu 0 0
cw_hooku
end
k = get cwtk 0
if eq k 0
ret
end
i = sub k 1
if or ne cw_g i 9 1 eq cw_g i 10 0
ret
end
if lt sub ulong monons get cwt0 i mul get cwtk 1 1000000
ret
end
for j ulong 64
if and eq get sjid j cw_g i 10 eq get sjst j 3
x = auth_cancel c j
if ge x 0
cw_ev i cw_g i 10 5 ulong x
put cwtk 0 0
end
end
end
end

note Test hook cwtu: SIGKILL the worker of the first replace, once, after its
note START is durable; whether the edit happened is then unknown to the
note creator and to the journal. A job is assigned (state 3) before its
note worker's proposal is decided and START journaled, so state 3 alone
note could kill a worker whose job holds ADMIT only (DRA-292, job 1054).
fn cw_hooku to void
for j ulong 64
if and and eq get sjst j 3 eq rem get sjid j 10 4 jn_started get sjid j
x = killpid int get swpid get sjw j 9
put cwtu 0 0
ret
end
end
end

fn cw_left to ulong
n = ulong 0
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
if eq cw_g i 12 0
n = add n 1
end
end
ret n
end

note Creator loop until every objective finished or dl ns pass: 0 or 62.
fn cw_drive c long dl ulong to int
for t ulong 1000000000
r = sched_step c 5000000
cw_coll c
k = auth_step c
cw_cmd c
cw_plan c
cw_vsnap c
if eq cw_left 0
ret 0
end
if ge ulong monons dl
ret 62
end
end
ret 62
end

note ======== creator: operator view and commands (DRA-291, seed/node/view.om)

note The snapshot: generic sections, then the objectives and the limits.
fn cw_vsnap c long to void
vw_begin
vw_gen c
vw_s 21 get cwpv 0
vw_s 128 get cwno 0
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
o = add 136 mul i 16
for w ulong 14
vw_s add o w cw_g i sub ulong get cwvw w 48
end
end
vw_s 200 7
vw_s 201 900
vw_s 202 160
vw_s 203 CWOBJ
vw_s 204 64
vw_s 205 256
vw_end
end

note One posted command: a committed id is acknowledged again as a
note duplicate; otherwise it is checked against the state the operator saw
note (stale, invalid), committed (OPER durable, then acted on), and
note acknowledged.
fn cw_cmd c long to void
d = new ulong 8 0
if not vw_take d
ret
end
k = jn_ofind get d 0
if ge k 0
vw_ack 4 jn_opw ulong k 7 get jseq 0
ret
end
st = cw_cchk d
if eq st 0
st = cw_exec c d
end
if eq st 0
vw_cnt 1 add vw_cget 1 1
vw_cnt 3 get d 0
vw_ack 0 jn_opw ulong jn_ofind get d 0 7 get jseq 0
ret
end
vw_cnt 2 add vw_cget 2 1
vw_ack st vw_ver get jseq 0
end

note 0 when command d (id, op, target, version, a..d) may run now; 1 stale
note (what it targets changed after the version the operator saw, or the
note version is not of this incarnation), 2 invalid.
fn cw_cchk d view ulong 8 to ulong
op = get d 1
t = get d 2
if eq get d 3 not ulong 0
ret 2
end
if gt get d 3 vw_ver
ret 1
end
if or eq op 1 eq op 2
if gt get cwpv 0 get d 3
ret 1
end
if eq get scpause 0 sub 2 op
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
if or or lt op 3 gt op 5 ge t get cwno 0
ret 2
end
if gt cw_g t 17 get d 3
ret 1
end
if eq cw_g t 9 4
ret 2
end
if and eq op 4 gt get d 4 7
ret 2
end
if eq op 5
ret cw_rchk d
end
ret 0
end

fn cw_rchk d view ulong 8 to ulong
if or lt get d 4 1 gt get d 4 3
ret 2
end
for m ulong 3
if gt get d add 5 m 99
ret 2
end
end
ret 0
end

note Commit command d: pause and resume go through auth_pause (which
note journals PAUSE) and are then recorded; objective commands are recorded
note (OPER durable) and then applied. 0, or 3 refused.
fn cw_exec c long d view ulong 8 to ulong
a = new ulong 4 0
for m ulong 4
put a m get d add 4 m
end
op = get d 1
v = add vw_ver 1
if le op 2
x = auth_pause c eq op 1
if ne get jbad 0 0
ret 3
end
end
if ne jn_oper get d 0 op get d 2 a v 0
ret 3
end
x = vw_ev 3 get d 2 op get d 0 0
if le op 2
put cwpv 0 vw_ev 4 0 0 sub 2 op 0
ret 0
end
cw_apply c get d 2 op a
ret 0
end

note Apply objective command op to objective i (also when the journal is
note replayed at a restart, when nothing is in flight).
fn cw_apply c long i ulong op ulong a view ulong 4 to void
if eq op 4
cw_s i 16 get a 0
cw_s i 17 vw_ver
ret
end
if eq op 5
for m ulong 4
cw_s i m get a m
end
end
if eq cw_g i 10 0
if eq op 3
cw_end i 19
else
cw_redo i
end
cw_s i 17 vw_ver
ret
end
if eq op 3
cw_s i 19 1
else
cw_s i 18 1
end
cw_s i 17 vw_ver
cw_stop c cw_g i 10
end

note Cancel job id through the authority wherever it is (waiting, ready or
note running); its result then reaches cw_oper.
fn cw_stop c long id ulong to void
for j ulong 64
s = get sjst j
if and eq get sjid j id and ge s 1 le s 3
x = auth_cancel c j
end
end
end

note At a restart: the committed operator commands again, in order.
fn cw_replay c long to void
a = new ulong 4 0
for k ulong jn_nops bound 128
for m ulong 4
put a m jn_opw k add 3 m
end
op = jn_opw k 1
i = jn_opw k 2
if and ge op 3 lt i get cwno 0
if ne cw_g i 9 4
cw_apply c i op a
end
end
vw_cnt 1 add vw_cget 1 1
vw_cnt 3 jn_opw k 0
end
end

note ======== worker

note Worker w: the input of its job (objective i): the newest version on the
note objective's topic that is not newer than the assignment's version.
fn cw_input c long w ulong i ulong dst edit uchar 4096 to long
v = sc_cell w 24
t = shl ulong 1 i
h = pool_hold c w sc_cell w 16
if le h 0
ret neg long 1
end
cur = ulong 0
last = ulong 0
for k ulong 65
x = node_next h cur t
if le x 0
break
end
if gt ulong x v
break
end
last = ulong x
cur = last
end
n = neg long 1
if gt last 0
n = node_read h last dst
end
r = pool_release c w
ret n
end

note Worker w, assignment q: propose, wait for the decision, run the child
note when granted, report. Outcome word: the authority's outcome (0 UNKNOWN,
note 1 not performed, 2 performed) plus the wait status shifted by 8; 16 +
note verdict when refused; 90 when the input was not found.
fn cw_job c long w ulong q ulong to void
pk = new uchar 4096 0
op = new ulong 4 0
id = sc_cell w 8
n = cw_input c w sub div id 1000 1 pk
if le n 0
r = sched_wdone w q 90 pk 0
ret
end
put op 0 id
put op 1 rem id 10
put op 2 div id 1000
put op 3 1
r = auth_propose w q op cw_class id
v = auth_wdecide c w q 30000000000
if ne v 0
r = sched_wdone w q add 16 ulong v pk 0
ret
end
cw_wrun c w q pk ulong n
end

note Replace changes the workspace (class 1); the others are rerunnable.
fn cw_class id ulong to ulong
if eq rem id 10 4
ret 1
end
ret 2
end

fn cw_wrun c long w ulong q ulong pk view uchar 4096 n ulong to void
ob = new uchar 4096 0
o = auth_wtool c w q pk n cw_class sc_cell w 8
r = auth_wreport w q ulong o
m = auth_wout w ob
x = or ulong o shl auth_cell w 96 8
r = sched_wdone w q x ob m
end

fn cw_worker c long w ulong to int
for it ulong 1000000000
q = sched_wjob w
if gt q 0
cw_job c w q
end
r = auth_wwait c w neg int 1 1000000000
if or eq r 2 eq r 3
ret 0
end
if eq r 4
t = auth_wctl w
end
if lt r 0
ret 45
end
end
ret 46
end

note ======== setup

note Objective argument "KIND,K,N,A,PATH,TASK" (KIND add, mul or loop) into
note slot i. false when malformed.
fn cw_parse i ulong a view uchar * to bool
f = new ulong 8 0
cw_s i 16 7
k = ulong 0
for j ulong len a
if and lt k 5 eq get a j 44
put f k j
k = add k 1
end
end
if ne k 5
ret false
end
if cw_eq view part a 0 get f 0 cwadd
cw_s i 0 1
end
if cw_eq view part a 0 get f 0 cwmul
cw_s i 0 2
end
if cw_eq view part a 0 get f 0 cwloop
cw_s i 0 3
end
if eq cw_g i 0 0
ret false
end
for m ulong 3
v = cw_pnum a add get f m 1 get f add m 1
if gt v 99
ret false
end
cw_s i add m 1 v
end
ret cw_ptxt i a f
end

fn cw_pnum a view uchar * s ulong e ulong to ulong
if or ge s e gt sub e s 2
ret 999
end
v = ulong 0
for j ulong sub e s
c = ulong get a add s j
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret 999
end
v = add mul v 10 sub c 48
end
ret v
end

note PATH and TASK of the objective argument a (field ends in f).
fn cw_ptxt i ulong a view uchar * f view ulong 8 to bool
ps = add get f 3 1
pn = sub get f 4 ps
ts = add get f 4 1
tn = sub len a ts
if or or eq pn 0 gt pn 128 or eq tn 0 gt tn 383
ret false
end
cw_put add mul i 512 0 view part a ps pn
cw_put add mul i 512 128 view part a ts tn
cw_s i 4 pn
cw_s i 5 tn
ret true
end

fn cw_put o ulong a view uchar * to void
for j ulong len a
put cwos add o j get a j
end
end

note Argument ai into config slot k; false when empty or over 1000 bytes.
fn cw_carg ai ulong k ulong to bool
n = argread ai cwcf mul k 1024 1000
if lt n 1
ret false
end
put cwcl k ulong n
ret true
end

note Next job seq and performed model turns of objective i from the journal.
fn cw_resume i ulong to void
s = ulong 0
t = ulong 0
for q ulong 99
for kd ulong 5
id = add add mul add i 1 1000 mul q 10 add kd 1
if jn_known id
s = add q 1
if and eq kd 0 eq and jn_jout id 255 2
t = add t 1
end
end
end
end
cw_s i 11 s
cw_s i 7 t
end

note FNV-1a 64 of the objective arguments, for the journal's identity.
fn cw_ident a0 ulong n ulong to ulong
b = new uchar 1024 0
x = ulong 14695981039346656037
for i ulong n
m = argread add a0 i b 0 1024
for j ulong ulong m
x = mul xor x ulong get b j 1099511628211
end
x = mul xor x 255 1099511628211
end
ret x
end

note The journal's objective: tag 0x4f4d4e43 ("OMNC"), the objective count,
note the hash of the objective arguments, the issue number.
fn cw_jopen ai ulong n ulong to ulong
d = new uchar 128 0
o = new ulong 4 0
for j ulong get cwcl 5 bound 128
put d j get cwcf add 5120 j
end
put o 0 1330466371
put o 1 n
put o 2 cw_ident ai n
put o 3 290
ret jn_open d get cwcl 5 o 3000
end

note Make WORK/o<i> for every objective (an existing one is reused).
fn cw_dirs to void
t = new uchar 4096 0
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
n = cw_wdir t i
x = makedir t 0 n 448
end
end

note omnode-code INFER TOOL OMC ROOT WORK JDIR PORT VIEW OBJ... from
note argument k on (1..4 objectives; all paths absolute; VIEW the operator
note view's port on 127.0.0.1, 0 for none). Exit 0 all passed, 1 some
note failed, 2 usage, 62 out of time, 30 + journal refusal, 50.. setup (57
note a job left waiting or ready by the last creator could not be cancelled).
fn cw_main k ulong dls ulong to int
b = new uchar 1024 0
c = ulong argcnt
if or lt c add k 9 gt c add k 12
ret 2
end
for a ulong 8
if not cw_carg add k a a
ret 2
end
end
if gt cw_cnum 7 65535
ret 2
end
put cwno 0 sub c add k 8
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
m = argread add add k 8 i b 0 1024
if lt m 1
ret 2
end
if not cw_parse i view part b 0 ulong m
ret 2
end
end
ret cw_run k dls
end

note Config slot k as a decimal of 1..5 digits; 99999999 otherwise.
fn cw_cnum k ulong to ulong
n = get cwcl k
if or eq n 0 gt n 5
ret 99999999
end
v = ulong 0
for j ulong n
d = ulong get cwcf add mul k 1024 j
if or lt d 48 gt d 57
ret 99999999
end
v = add mul v 10 sub d 48
end
ret v
end

fn cw_run k ulong dls ulong to int
c = pool_new 4 2
if le c 0
ret 50
end
if ne sup_init c 0
ret 51
end
ql = get cwql 0
if eq ql 0
ql = 8
end
if ne sched_new c ql 8 0
ret 52
end
if ne auth_new c 0
ret 53
end
e = cw_jopen add k 8 get cwno 0
if ne e 0
ret int add 30 e
end
e = auth_recover c
if ne e 0
ret int add 30 e
end
for j ulong 64
s = get sjst j
if or eq s 1 eq s 2
if lt auth_cancel c j 0
ret 57
end
end
end
if ne vw_new jn_fence 0
ret 55
end
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
cw_resume i
if ne jn_res i 0
cw_s i 7 jn_rturn i
cw_pub i jn_res i
end
end
cw_replay c
cw_dirs
for w ulong 2
p = auth_spawn c w
if eq p 0
exit cw_worker c w
end
if le p 0
ret 54
end
end
if not cw_view c
ret 56
end
r = cw_drive c add ulong monons mul dls 1000000000
vw_stop
x = sched_stop c 2000000000
sup_closeall
jn_close
ret cw_sum r
end

note Start the view process when VIEW is not 0 and print CWV port once it
note listens; false when it could not.
fn cw_view c long to bool
o = new uchar 4096 0
pt = cw_cnum 7
if eq pt 0
ret true
end
cw_vsnap c
if le vw_spawn pt 0
ret false
end
for t ulong 3000
if ne vw_g 7 0
p = cw_cat o 0 cwcwv
p = cw_dec o p vw_g 7
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
cw_out o p
ret true
end
x = sleepns 1000000
end
vw_stop
ret false
end

fn cw_sum r int to int
o = new uchar 4096 0
np = ulong 0
for i ulong get cwno 0 bound 4
if eq cw_g i 12 1
np = add np 1
end
end
p = cw_cat o 0 cwsum
p = cw_dec o p np
p = cw_cat o p cwsumf
p = cw_dec o p sub get cwno 0 np
p = cw_cat o p cwnl
cw_out o p
if ne r 0
ret r
end
if eq np get cwno 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
